cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use FlyGI, please cite the paper given under preferred-citation, and
  also cite the MaleCNS connectome it is built on (listed under references):
  "Sexual dimorphism in the complete Drosophila male central nervous system
  connectome", Cell 189 (2026), doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.08.015.
title: FlyGI
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - given-names: Mustafa
    family-names: Safdari
    alias: msafdari
repository-code: "https://github.com/msafdari/FlyGI"
abstract: >-
  FlyGI is an experimental framework for testing whether the topology of the
  MaleCNS v1.0 fruit-fly connectome offers measurable advantages on interactive
  ARC-AGI-3 tasks relative to matched graph controls.
license: MIT-0
keywords:
  - ARC-AGI-3
  - connectome
  - Drosophila
  - reservoir computing
  - reproducible research
preferred-citation:
  type: report
  title: >-
    I Wired a Whole Fly Brain into ARC-AGI-3. It Lost All Season, Then Won
    One Back
  authors:
    - given-names: Mustafa
      family-names: Safdari
      alias: Megus Alexandrus
  year: 2026
  institution:
    name: Kaggle
  publisher:
    name: Kaggle
  doi: 10.34740/kaggle/w/116268
  url: "https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/arc-prize-2026-paper-track/writeups/flygi-connectome-attribution-audit"
  notes: >-
    Kaggle Writeup submitted to the ARC Prize 2026 Paper Track. Kaggle
    registered the DOI on 2026-11-10 (UTC). The DOI record lists the author
    under the Kaggle display name Megus Alexandrus.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Sexual dimorphism in the complete Drosophila male central nervous
      system connectome
    authors:
      - name: FlyEM at HHMI Janelia
      - name: University of Cambridge Department of Zoology
      - name: MRC Laboratory of Molecular Biology
      - name: Google Research
    journal: Cell
    volume: 189
    issue: 18
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.1016/j.cell.2026.08.015
    notes: >-
      MaleCNS v1.0 dataset, released 2026-06-08 under CC BY 4.0. The author
      list here names the collaborating institutions as given in this
      repository's README; use the paper's own author list (via the DOI) when
      citing it. FlyGI runtime assets are modified derivatives, neither an
      official release nor endorsed by the data creators.
